solution_steps:
When dividing $10x^3 - 7x^2 + ax + 6$ by $2x^2 - 3x + 1$ using long division, we get
\[
\begin{array}{c|cc cc}
& 5x & +3 \\
\cline{2-5}
2x^2 - 3x + 1 & 10x^3 & -7x^2 & +ax & +6 \\
& -10x^3 & +15x^2 & -5x & \\
\cline{2-4}
& & 8x^2 & +(a-5)x & +6 \\
& & -8x^2 & +12x & -4 \\
\cline{3-5}
& & & (a-5+12)x & +2 \\
\end{array}
\]
Since the remainder remains constant regardless of the value of $x$, the coefficient of $x$ in the remainder, $(a-5+12)$, must be equal to zero. Therefore, we have $(a-5+12)x+2=0$. Since this equation holds for all values of $x$, the coefficient of $x$ must be zero. Thus, we have $a-5+12=0$, which gives $a=\boxed{-7}$.The answer is: -7

