Let
\[f(a,b) = \left\{
\renewcommand{\arraystretch}{3}
\begin{array}{cl}
\dfrac{ab - a + 2}{2a} & \text{if $a + b \le 3$}, \\
\dfrac{ab - b - 2}{-2b} & \text{if $a + b > 3$}.
\end{array}
\renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1}
\right.\]Find $f(2,1) + f(2,4).$

solution_steps:
Consider the expansion of $(2 - 3)^{1990}$. By the Binomial Theorem, the sum of the coefficients of the even-powered terms is equal to the sum of the coefficients of the odd-powered terms. In other words,
\begin{align*} \frac{(2 - 3)^{1990} + (2 + 3)^{1990}}{2} &= \sum_{n = 0}^{995} (-3)^n \binom{1990}{2n} + \sum_{n = 0}^{995} 3^n \binom{1990}{2n} \\ &= \sum_{n = 0}^{995} (-3)^n \binom{1990}{2n} + \sum_{n = 0}^{995} 3^n \binom{1990}{1990 - 2n} \\ &= \sum_{n = 0}^{995} (-3)^n \binom{1990}{2n} + \sum_{n = 995}^{1990} (-1)^n \binom{1990}{n} \\ &= \sum_{n = 0}^{995} (-3)^n \binom{1990}{2n} + \sum_{n = 0}^{995} (-1)^n \binom{1990}{n}. \end{align*}
But the left-hand side is simply $\left(\frac{2-3}{2}\right)^{1990} = \left(-\frac{1}{2}\right)^{1990}$. Therefore,
\[\sum_{n = 0}^{995} (-3)^n \binom{1990}{2n} + \sum_{n = 0}^{995} (-1)^n \binom{1990}{n} = \left(-\frac{1}{2}\right)^{1990}.\]
Since we are asked to find $\frac{1}{2^{1990}} \sum_{n = 0}^{995} (-3)^n \binom{1990}{2n}$, we multiply both sides by $2^{1990}$ to get
\[\sum_{n = 0}^{995} (-3)^n \binom{1990}{2n} = \frac{1}{2^{1990}} \cdot \left(-\frac{1}{2}\right)^{1990} = \boxed{-\frac{1}{2}}.\]The answer is: -\frac{1}{2}

