To convert $\frac{37}{80}$ to a decimal, we divide 37 by 80:
\[
\begin{array}{c|cccc}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{0.} & 4 & 6 & 2 \\
\cline{2-5}
80 & 3 & 7 & . & 0 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{3} & 2 & 0 & \\
\cline{2-3}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 5 & 0 & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 4 & 0 & \\
\cline{3-4}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 1 & 0 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 8 & 0 \\
\cline{4-5}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & & 2 \\
\end{array}
\]
Therefore, $\frac{37}{80}$ as a terminating decimal is $\boxed{0.4625}$.The answer is: 0.4625

